rt+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"4ae34c4c28a086ab62b8491a4b05530bc52b68ff9a716592fd010586c69f488d","event_uuid":"4618aede-0fe1-4891-a3aa-26b151420177","position":{"commit_sha":"9010913a46ddb03cfcf58b9495d7614a49519bb2","position":"1788871698213229001-4618aede-0fe1-4891-a3aa-26b151420177"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e81b74670d099ecd9b9d9e9f18ebd5936f578235eb567a9754e5cb28fbe72ed2","event_uuid":"cdae7b7b-0479-4461-8ce2-505a2092f932","position":{"commit_sha":"ca02b51da75312506ff2078078b19acf5449b28d","position":"1788872265390073001-cdae7b7b-0479-4461-8ce2-505a2092f932"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8a219fa3a26639c23964f347791d2d1306f784b731e76a20b96c5fed6b7e2c7e","event_uuid":"a6bd0bb9-2408-4b35-842b-ceb8754ebcdd","position":{"commit_sha":"11415c7c5b115028f562b295fe1fd576bba177f1","position":"1788872290339427001-a6bd0bb9-2408-4b35-842b-ceb8754ebcdd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed to Gerrit change 2831. RCA: plan-review close recheck ran before close-class/reason-backed administrative disposition evidence was validated/threaded, so task --class obsolete --reason fell through to a normal plan-review attestation check and failed unsigned. RED: tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py::test_open_task_obsolete_close_bypasses_plan_review_close_gate failed before the fix with the plan-review attestation error. Fix: validate close-class evidence before the close gate, pass close_reason into the plan-review close check, reuse close_disposition.verdict as the evidence predicate, and preserve normal completed-work close gating. Validation: focused close-gate suite passed; make verify passed with GIT_CONFIG_* unset.","timestamp":1788868211950620001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788814223700006001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dbee09a8-5674-49d3-aa24-8f93720039a8","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"192c-d606-b72e-470f"},{"link_uuid":"34de4ea9-07a1-406c-bcfc-46cf8de8602c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"048d-49f2-bd55-4357"}],"description":"## Observation\nThe force-close hint advertises a no-force path for administrative dispositions:\n> Hint: if this close is administrative (duplicate / obsolete / superseded / wontfix rather than completed work), --class <value> closes it through the attested disposition path — obsolete/wontfix with --reason=<text> ... no --force needed.\n\nBut in practice on task ticket 192c-d606-b72e-470f (brokendown-graceless-pelican, invalid premise), `rebar transition <id> open closed --class obsolete --reason=...` fails with `plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation`. A signed BLOCK plan-review still cannot satisfy the gate, so invalid-premise task tickets are structurally unclosable without operator force. Bug-type administrative closes have been observed to close gate-free through the same --class path.\n\n## Prior-art decision to revise\nBug 69b9 deliberately exempted only link-backed administrative classes (`duplicate`, `superseded`) from the plan-review close gate because those have verifiable replacement-link evidence. Since then, `close_disposition.verdict()` gained deterministic reason-backed disposition attestations for `obsolete` and `wontfix`: the close reason is recorded as `close_reason` and signed into the completion-verifier/disposition manifest. This ticket does not add a plain prose-only bypass; it extends the plan-review close gate to recognize the same deterministic disposition attestation that the completion close path already mints, and it must validate class/reason/replacement requirements before granting the exemption.\n\n## Hypothesis\nThe plan-review close gate runs before the completion precheck's close-class validation and its exemption predicate only checks `_LINK_BACKED_DISPOSITION_CLASSES`. Therefore reason-backed administrative dispositions reach the plan-review gate as ordinary completed-work closes and fail on missing PASS plan-review. The fix is to (1) run the shared `txn.close_class_refusal()` validation before the plan-review close recheck, (2) thread `close_reason` into `_plan_review_close_recheck()` / `gates.close_plan_review_gate_check()`, and (3) have the gate reuse `close_disposition.verdict()` for all administrative classes so obsolete/wontfix are exempt only when a signable reason-backed disposition exists.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py -q` includes a RED regression where an open task with plan-review close gate enabled closes as `--class obsolete --reason=...` without `--force`; before the fix it raises the plan-review attestation error, after the fix it succeeds and records `close_class=obsolete` plus the reason-backed disposition attestation.\n- [x] Completed-work closes without `--class` still require the existing certified plan-review/completion-verifier path; the regression suite proves that normal closes are not weakened.\n- [x] Administrative disposition closes (`obsolete`, `wontfix`, `duplicate`, `superseded`) bypass the plan-review close gate for non-bug and bug tickets only after `txn.close_class_refusal()` / `close_disposition.verdict()` accepts the class/reason/replacement evidence.\n- [x] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` and the CLI hint agree that administrative/attested-disposition closes do not need force and do not require a PASSING plan-review attestation.\n\n## Testing\n- RED/GREEN: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py -q`\n- Focused full close-path coverage: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py tests/unit/test_close_gate_disposition_69b9.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_transition_reason_honest_3803.py -q`\n- Full verification before push: `env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_2 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_2 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/gates.py","reason":"plan-review close gate exemption for administrative disposition classes"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"administrative disposition attestation path close semantics"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"close gate ordering around disposition closes"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"document administrative close gate bypass behavior"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py","reason":"regression coverage for open task administrative close bypass and normal close gate preservation"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","048d-49f2-bd55-4357"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"cdae7b7b-0479-4461-8ce2-505a2092f932","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1b22-0e6a-1d49-44be","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Administrative close (--class obsolete/wontfix) still demands plan-review attestation, contradicting its own hint","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c673fa18-0941-4c92-ad90-eb16eb168977","b23f4939-c109-4f37-95e6-0be9a3f0c5fa","5ef092f0-8b12-4202-8c4e-a490082ccf4e","d00dae25-4244-490f-ba0f-2e495d4c8e4b","517254a9-be11-4679-99e8-3834d5922e4f","f9811c44-a454-4a31-9dd8-89002a4edd36","730a7d91-d568-4cee-97a3-86016667f7b5","34de4ea9-07a1-406c-bcfc-46cf8de8602c","4618aede-0fe1-4891-a3aa-26b151420177","cdae7b7b-0479-4461-8ce2-505a2092f932","a6bd0bb9-2408-4b35-842b-ceb8754ebcdd"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788884960990528001,"uuid":"96e75b35-f8fd-45cd-be43-cc86def21466"}